{
 "_doc": "What an OpenStreetMap place is in the game (tools/osm2gltf.py writes <map>.places.json from it; main.gd reads both). match: OSM tag -> values. label: shown in the editor and the tablet. icon: the tablet's map pictogram (gadgets/tablet/ui/map/<icon>.png). pickup: a role (roles.json) or item id put at its door, respawning. sign: a sign on its facade. model: a hand-made model placed there when the place is not a building (a fuel station's forecourt). interior: an interior set (layout.json) for a small one-storey shop: the building becomes a walk-in shell (walls, shop window, door, a sign with the place's name) with that furniture inside. caption: the sign's text when OSM has no name. storefront: generic shop models (common/storefronts, %s = front width in metres) - shop: a whole one-storey shop, widths; a small shop building gets the widest that fits, the rest of its footprint stays a building. module: the street-level shop module for a taller building (its front just outside the facade).",
